    "body": "Quick pass (coordinator, read only, no build) on head `81a919838`: the PR is a sub-PR of `side/path-kernel` and merges cleanly with it (`21fd9e57d`, merged in). The body starts with `Side branch: side/path-kernel`, maps each item of class B of the review of PR #4383 to its commit, and has `Refs #4407` and `Refs #4383`. The writer records on #4407 are released. The PR is flagged ready. It waits for the independent review.\n\nGate state, as the author reports it:\n- The full batch (1234 steps, 0 failed) ran on the head `fddbabe3b`, before the merge of the side branch and before the last commit.\n- On this head: `cargo check --tests` and clippy for pathkernel and motion, the pathkernel `laws` suite, and the motion kernel tests pass.\n- Not run on this head: the full batch, the light lane, and the app check. A sync worker runs the full batch, the heavy `motion` and `app` steps and the light lane on the final tree of the side branch immediately after this PR merges; those are the merge gates of PR #4383.\n\nNotes for the reviewer. The safety floor applies: these places decide entries, exits and retracts.\n- The rule of the class: never recover silently from a rejected result; refuse by name, or record the fallback with a note. Check each row of the table in the body, and the search for the rest of the class.\n- `Exit::new` now takes the material top and refuses a retract under it (the work of #4415, which is closed).\n- The PR points about 50 citations of the removed record file to `RECOMMENDED.md` (heading `#4024`) and adds `docs/decisions/4407-pathkernel-dependency-edges.md`.\n- Check that each changed reading of the kernel tables is a measured value with its cause.",
